59:   reflect) are met each unit: ask and find in the plan and search (unit 1), judge in purpose and kind (unit 2), use in
60:   answer-only notes (unit 2) and the survey tally (unit 3), share and reflect in each unit's close and in unit 4's
61:   feedback round.
62: - **Evidence.** Daily: an exit ticket that asks the student to do the unit's move once on a new case (about 5
63:   minutes, all at once), with error letters for the usual slips; on inquiry days, the working notes in the research
64:   notebook (APPROACH.md). End-of-unit assessment: a written sitting on a case not seen before, all 30 at once, scored
65:   on a short teacher-judged rubric plus a few one-answer items checked on the page, in about 20 to 27 minutes; unit
66:   4 adds its revised product, scored on its rubric after the feedback round and revision counted in its days. Each
