3-inquiry-questions, in the same weeks, on its town topic; stand-alone: "How do spiders catch their food?" | First because every later unit starts from a research question the student wrote; the first weeks are when social studies grade 3 also teaches compelling and supporting questions (one class question can serve both) | Candidate: the continuum's grade 3 background cell (a teacher-given source before the questions) at the inquiry day's opening; its grade 3 predict cell (what the new information may show) as one line on the question sheet | Neutral topic (spiders; the town's place is the host's question). A student who cannot think of a question may choose from three on a card. Whose voices: the unit records the makers of its passages and pictures (C12) |
