## Questions for Cory

1. **Q1, the excluded ids.** STANDARD.md section 4 excludes V.C.2 as a design cycle and III.A.1 as a relationship
   skill. By the framework, V.C.2 is building new ways to investigate together and III.A.1 is wanting to broaden and
   deepen understanding (both research), while V.B.2 (tinkering and making) is the design strand beside V.B.1.
   Recommended: exclude V.B.2 instead of V.C.2, keep III.A.1 in library (met through a research task), and describe
   III.D.2 as SEL social awareness, so six ids are excluded, not seven.
2. **Q2, the catalogue.** data/courses.csv has one `library` k-12 row; the settled list is eight courses.
   Recommended: eight rows matching the course ids.
3. **Q3, swapping and leaving out.** No library page says what a school may swap or leave out. Recommended: the SEL,
   PE and arts rule (swapping a case keeps its ids met; a left-out unit's ids are named as not claimed that year on
   the course page and in the family note), and K to 5 case sets stay off politics, elections, religion and conflict.

